# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the root one, so
# this scopes the ignore list to this image without adding a root .dockerignore
# that would change how anything else in the repo is built.
#
# The image needs exactly two things out of the repository:
#   scripts/black-reports/   the generator
#   render-service/          this service
# Everything else is excluded so no application source, no test fixture and no
# local .env can end up in a layer.
*
!scripts/black-reports/**
!render-service/requirements.txt
!render-service/wsgi.py
